+> The examples below use a hardcoded value so they stay readable, but in a real app load a randomly generated secret of at least 32 characters from an environment variable such as `process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD`, and never commit it to source control. A guessable passphrase (even one ≥32 characters) is not safe. When rotating the password, see "Rotating passwords" below: the previous password should be removed from the list once the transition is over, since anyone holding it can still forge sessions.
 
